      "id": 1,
      "text": "Compton was founded when the railroad bypassed Melugin’s Grove in 1872, prompting residents to move and establish the village named after Joel Compton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.shawlocal.com/sauk-valley-living/family/2025/12/16/a-good-place-to-live-compton-observes-150th-anniversary/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village celebrated its 150th anniversary on July 19‑20 with a craft show, kids activities, a time capsule, and a park dedication to Village President Donald “Doc” Swope.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.shawlocal.com/sauk-valley-living/family/2025/12/16/a-good-place-to-live-compton-observes-150th-anniversary/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Compton’s Community Club, founded in 1946, is the oldest such organization in Illinois, coordinating many local events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.shawlocal.com/sauk-valley-living/family/2025/12/16/a-good-place-to-live-compton-observes-150th-anniversary/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The post office that opened in 1841 was originally called Melugin Grove, named after early settler Zachariah Melugin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
